;; Eager-core POLICY (design §6) — the eager-core is a declared predicate over
;; the single-source catalog-model, NOT a hand-listed set.  The generator emits
;; the `ToolSearch select:...` block by applying this policy to the CURRENT
;; catalog, so when consolidation collapses verbs the block regenerates to
;; reference the merged verbs automatically — no hand-edit, no drift.
;;
;; MECHANISM vs MEMBERSHIP (design §6, open question #1):
;;   F6 delivers the MECHANISM (policy-as-data -> generated block, gate-checked).
;;   The final 12-15 membership is a Dan-/consolidation-gated decision that
;;   depends on the consolidated catalog (which does not exist yet).  Two
;;   ratified decisions disagree on the size (Alt-D ADR + live memory-open = 22;
;;   W4.5 = 12-15); the re-scope decision rules "derive from the consolidated
;;   catalog, don't hand-prune."  Until that catalog exists, this policy
;;   REPRODUCES the current live 22-verb eager-core so the drift gate has a
;;   stable, faithful baseline — it is deliberately NOT the future 12-15 set.
;;
;; Policy evaluation (applied by the generator):
;;   1. :verbs-eager  — explicit verb names always in the eager core (order
;;      preserved as listed here — the block is order-sensitive for humans).
;;   2. :verbs-demoted — verbs FORCIBLY EXCLUDED even if a future :axes-eager
;;      rule would include them (encodes the composition doctrine's explicit
;;      "DEMOTE navigate.path-via OUT of the eager core", model-mount decision
;;      Part 2 — so the demotion can't silently regress).
;;   3. The generator asserts every :verbs-eager name EXISTS in the model
;;      (a rename/removal that orphans an eager-core entry FAILS the gate).
;;
;; The ToolSearch wire form is mcp__sandbar__sandbar_<axis>_<leaf> with the
;; verb's dots after the axis turned to underscores in the LEAF only
;; (sandbar.navigate.outbound-edges -> mcp__sandbar__sandbar_navigate_outbound-edges).

{;; The current live eager-core, verbatim from memory-open.md:35 (22 verbs).
 ;; Order matches the live block exactly (drift-gate baseline).
 :verbs-eager
 ["sandbar.entity.find"
  "sandbar.entity.find-by-rel-path"
  "sandbar.entity.create"
  "sandbar.entity.update"
  "sandbar.entity.validate"
  "sandbar.search.bm25f"
  "sandbar.search.attribute"
  "sandbar.aggregate.count"
  "sandbar.aggregate.group-by"
  "sandbar.aggregate.rank-by"
  "sandbar.navigate.outbound-edges"
  "sandbar.navigate.inbound-edges"
  "sandbar.navigate.siblings-of"
  "sandbar.navigate.path-via"
  "sandbar.orient.library-card"
  "sandbar.ground"
  "sandbar.workflow.define"
  "sandbar.workflow.find"
  "sandbar.workflow.start-process"
  "sandbar.workflow.transition"
  "sandbar.workflow.process-state"
  "sandbar.workflow.orchestrate"]

 ;; FUTURE demotions (design §6 + model-mount Part 2).  Empty today because the
 ;; live block still includes path-via; the consolidation front flips this to
 ;; #{"sandbar.navigate.path-via"} when it derives the 12-15 set.  Encoded as
 ;; data so the demotion is enforceable by the generator, not prose.
 :verbs-demoted #{}}
